//! tr kodlu 1
// 18 — Modules: splitting code into files and importing them.
// What it teaches: import to use the names in another .tr file, as to give an alias (avoids name clashes).
// Imported file: helpers/geometry.tr.
// Builds on: functions (08) and tests (17); a module is a file that holds functions and constants.
// Run (from the project root): tr examples/en/18_modules.tr

A070 "helpers/geometry" // the .tr extension is optional; names are used directly
G100("area of a circle with r = 2: {G405(circle_area(2), 3)}")

A070 "helpers/geometry" A100 geo // with an alias: geo.name
G100("geo.PI = {geo.PI}")
G100("area of a circle with r = 1: {G405(geo.circle_area(1), 3)}")

// --- Try it yourself ---
// 1. Add a rectangle_area(width, depth) function to helpers/geometry.tr and call it from here.
// 2. Import the same module under two different aliases and check that both give the same PI.
